  "title": "Ride-Sharing Trip & Payment Fix",
  "diagramType": "er",
  "type": "fix",
  "difficulty": "Intermediate",
  "category": "Entity-Relationship",
  "scenario": "A ride-sharing database mistakenly links Payment directly to Driver instead of Trip, and Driver is missing its link to Trip.",
  "goal": "Repair the trip ledger so Payment settles a single Trip (1:1) rather than linking directly to Driver, and connect all Trip participants.",
  "learningObjective": "Attach transaction entities to the Trip event and distinguish 1:1 unique foreign keys from 1:N relationships.",
  "hints": [
    "Look for an edge that links Payment directly to a participant instead of Trip.",
    "Notice trip_id on Payment is UNIQUE — that means one Trip maps to one Payment (1:1).",
    "Delete Driver -> Payment, then connect Driver -> Trip (1:N) and Trip -> Payment (1:1)."
  ],
  "solutionExplanation": "Rider and Driver both participate in Trip (1:N), and Payment settles a specific Trip.",
  "initialNodes": [
